#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# unitize

#% text
# `unitize(x)` gives 0 when `x` is zero and 1 otherwise; `unitize(x, d)` gives 0 when `abs(x) < d`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Lists are taken element by element.

#% item
# A numeric expression is decided rigorously: a 30-digit enclosure that excludes 0 gives 1, `simplify` giving 0 gives 0; when neither decides, the call stays unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
unitize([[1, 0, 2], [0.0, -3, 0]])
#% output
#= [[1, 0, 1], [0, 1, 0]]

#% cell
unitize(pi)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
unitize(sqrt(2) + sqrt(3) - sqrt(5 + 2*sqrt(6)))
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
unitize([e, pi], 3)
#% output
#= [0, 1]

#% cell
unitize(x)
#% output
#= unitize(x)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `sign`, `chop`, `possible_zero_q`
